## Conjecture ledger

{{#if view.coordinator}}
- One file per conjecture in `wiki/conjectures/`: a connection between properties on a
  named family, tied to a question. Add one with the `new-conjecture` skill.
{{/if}}
{{#if view.coordinator}}
- Status is not the backlog. A line `@residue: <next step>` in a conjecture file marks work
  still to do; `bin/residues` lists them across all statuses. Keep refuted entries. Only {{owner}} writes `@priority`.
{{/if}}
{{#if view.shared}}
- Work that uses an argued claim or an open premise carries `@assumes: <C<nnn> or the
  argument file> — <the claim> — argued (<labels>)` where it uses it; `bin/residues --assumes` lists them.
{{/if}}
- Why and how: [docs/discipline/conjecture-ledger.md](docs/discipline/conjecture-ledger.md).
